From 7800ccee0160dba8c13fa8fed581bad29c9aeacd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ann-yanan <156587052+ann-yanan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 10:07:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] KVM: riscv: Sync next_cycles with VSTIMECMP updates

A guest using SBI TIME calls set_timer() to arm its next tick or a
wake-up deadline before entering WFI. The ecall exits to KVM.
kvm_riscv_vcpu_sync_interrupts() samples VSTIMECMP into
timer.next_cycles on VM exit, before kvm_riscv_vcpu_exit() handles the
SBI call, so next_cycles still contains the previous deadline (Told).

The SBI TIME handler passes the new deadline (Tnew) to
kvm_riscv_vcpu_update_vstimecmp(), which programs only the hardware
VSTIMECMP and leaves next_cycles at Told. The vCPU thread is a host
task and can be scheduled out before the next VM exit, for example when
its time slice expires, a higher-priority task wakes up, or it blocks.
kvm_arch_vcpu_put() then calls kvm_riscv_vcpu_timer_save(), which
disables VSTIMECMP. When the vCPU is loaded again,
kvm_riscv_vcpu_timer_restore() writes stale next_cycles (Told) back to
VSTIMECMP, overwriting Tnew. If the guest subsequently enters WFI, the
interrupt that should wake it at Tnew is lost and it can sleep
indefinitely.

This was reproduced with a two-vCPU nested-KVM WFI test guest running
on a four-vCPU PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Linux 7.2 L1 under QEMU TCG on x86_64.
The unpatched kernel intermittently stopped timer progress on both
vCPUs, or left only one vCPU making progress. TCG makes the scheduling
window easier to hit, but the stale software state and save/restore
sequence are independent of TCG.

Update next_cycles before programming VSTIMECMP, matching the existing
hrtimer update path, so vCPU put/load preserves the new deadline.

Testing:
- Two-vCPU SBI TIME/WFI stress on patched Linux 7.2 for 120 seconds:
  21086 timer wakeups total (vcpu0=10526, vcpu1=10560), wake_delays=0.
- Two-vCPU IRQFD/MSI WFI regression for 120 seconds: 44068/44068 MSIs
  injected/received, wake_delays=0, max_delay_ms=0, and no guest, vCPU,
  or injector errors.
- CubeSandbox control-plane on nested KVM: template creation, cold
  start, run_code, snapshot, warm restore, and filesystem/memory state
  validation passed both locally and in GitHub Actions.

Fixes: 8f5cb44b1bae ("RISC-V: KVM: Support sstc extension")
Assisted-by: Qoder
---
 arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu_timer.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu_timer.c b/arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu_timer.c
index a2cd277..9308067 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu_timer.c
+++ b/arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu_timer.c
@@ -75,6 +75,9 @@ static int kvm_riscv_vcpu_timer_cancel(struct kvm_vcpu_timer *t)
 
 static int kvm_riscv_vcpu_update_vstimecmp(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu, u64 ncycles)
 {
+	struct kvm_vcpu_timer *t = &vcpu->arch.timer;
+
+	t->next_cycles = ncycles;
 #if defined(CONFIG_32BIT)
 	ncsr_write(CSR_VSTIMECMP,  ULONG_MAX);
 	ncsr_write(CSR_VSTIMECMPH, ncycles >> 32);
-- 
